      "constraints": [
        "THIS BOX EXECUTES CODE IT IS SENT. Anyone who can reach its port can run anything its user can. Keep it on a trusted network; never publish the port.",
        "Field names come from the script's vs.emit calls, so data.out above is indicative - the reply's `encoding` map always names every field and its codec.",
        "A value that is neither an ndarray, bytes, nor JSON-serializable is refused; the box never pickles on a script's behalf.",
        "The image pins OpenCV below 5.0, because user code is overwhelmingly written against the 4.x API.",
        "Stateless. `reset` is accepted and does nothing; each request gets a fresh directory that is deleted afterwards."
      ],
      "path": "boxes/pycv"
    },
